  "id": "COMPOUND:11002 - PROTEIN:3858",
  "verbalization": "AGN-201904 is proposed to interact with Tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B through a series of molecular pathways involving retinoic acid receptors. The evidence suggests that AGN-201904 acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 3-hydroxyfriedel-3-en-2-one, sebacaldehyde, and deltonin, all of which are known to target retinoic acid receptor alpha. This indicates that AGN-201904 may be a modulator of the retinoic acid receptor alpha signaling pathway, which is involved in various cellular processes, including differentiation and apoptosis. The presence of multiple targets in this pathway suggests a potential role for AGN-201904 in regulating the activity of Tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B, possibly through the modulation of retinoic acid receptor alpha. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which AGN-201904 influences the function of Tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B, although further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
